-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 24: PREROGATIVE ORDERS (rules 1 to 6), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc6-order-23.l4.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that "means", a closing "only", a condition
--                introduced by "if", "where", "unless" or "only", a flat negative ("must not"), or a period
--                fixed in the text's own words and missed (ruling of 2026-11-05).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must", the
--                list is not closed, something lies outside the sources, or a grant ("may") is limited by its
--                own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every requirement here is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise (O 3 r 2(1)).
-- A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3 (roc1's range): each function takes the last day that Rule gives.

