-- The helper below is shared by paragraphs (2) and (6) of this Rule, Rule 5(5) and Rule 6(3): each says that a document must be
-- served "as soon as it is practicable ... and in any case no later than 2 working days after it is filed".
-- Fork F-O24-1: the sentence has two limbs.  Taken: the 2 working days are a backstop ("in any case"), so service after the last
-- day answers JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)) whatever else is true; service on or before it answers JUST TRUE when it was as
-- soon as practicable, and NOTHING otherwise, because "practicable" is a judgment the text leaves to the asker.  The other
-- reading is that service within the 2 working days is enough, so that it answers JUST TRUE whether or not it was as soon as practicable.
@ref O 24 r 4(2) (src:3766)
