      `it was served as soon as it was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 4(2) the document is served as soon as practicable and no later than 2 working days after it is filed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the document was served` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "in any case no later than 2 working days after it is filed"
        IF `it was served as soon as it was practicable` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "as soon as it is practicable" is a judgment the text leaves to the asker

@ref O 24 r 4(2) (src:3766)
