GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(3) the application for permission is made and supported as required` MEANS
    IF    `the application for permission is made by originating application`
      AND `a statement supports it` -- (a)
      AND `the statement sets out the name and description of the applicant, the relief sought and the grounds on which it is sought` -- (a)
      AND `an affidavit supports it` -- (b)
      AND `the affidavit shows that the applicant has the legal standing to make the application` -- (b)(i)
      AND `the affidavit shows that the evidence discloses an arguable case of reasonable suspicion in favour of the Court making the orders sought` -- (b)(ii)
      AND `the affidavit shows that the defendant and the matters in issue are susceptible to the orders sought` -- (b)(iii)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says how the application "must be made" and by what it "must be supported" and does not say what follows if not

-- src:3796 | (4) The applicant is bound by the grounds and relief set out in the statement and may not rely upon any ground or seek any relief, at any stage of the proceedings, that is not set out in the statement unless the Court otherwise allows.
@ref O 24 r 5(4) (src:3796)
GIVEN `the ground or relief is set out in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(4) the applicant may rely on the ground or seek the relief` MEANS
    IF `the ground or relief is set out in the statement` OR `the Court otherwise allows`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not rely upon any ground or seek any relief, at any stage of the proceedings, that is not set out in the statement unless the Court otherwise allows"

-- src:3797 | (5) The originating application, the statement and the affidavit must be served on the defendant and on the Attorney‑General as soon as is practicable after it is filed and in any case no later than 2 working days after it is filed.
@ref O 24 r 5(5) (src:3797)
GIVEN `the date the documents were served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `they were served as soon as it was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(5) the originating application, the statement and the affidavit are served on the defendant and the Attorney-General in time` MEANS
    `o 24 r 4(2) the document is served as soon as practicable and no later than 2 working days after it is filed` `the date the documents were served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `they were served as soon as it was practicable`

-- src:3798 | (6) The Attorney‑General may apply to the Court for an order that some other defendant be added or substituted as a party and that the Attorney‑General cease to be a defendant.
@ref O 24 r 5(6) (src:3798)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has been named as a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(6) the Attorney-General may apply to the Court for another defendant to be added or substituted` MEANS
    `o 24 r 4(4) the Attorney-General may apply to the Court for another defendant to be added or substituted` `the Attorney-General has been named as a defendant`

-- src:3799 | (7) The defendant and the Attorney‑General may file and serve affidavits to contest the application for permission and may make their affidavits jointly or separately.
@ref O 24 r 5(7) (src:3799)
GIVEN who IS A `o 24 r 4(5) who files an affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(7) the person may file and serve an affidavit to contest the application for permission` MEANS
    `o 24 r 4(5) the person may file and serve an affidavit to contest the summons` who

-- src:3800 | (8) The application for permission must be heard by a Judge.
@ref O 24 r 5(8) (src:3800)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(8) the application for permission is heard by a Judge` MEANS
    IF sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the application "must be heard by a Judge" and does not say what follows if another hears it

DECLARE `o 24 r 5(9) what the Court may order at the hearing` IS ONE OF
    `o 24 r 5(9)(a) the application be allowed`
    `o 24 r 5(9)(b) the application be dismissed`
    `o 24 r 5(9)(c) the application be served on some other persons`
    `o 24 r 5(9)(d) further affidavits be filed and served by the parties`
    `o 24 r 5(9) something else`

-- src:3801 | (9) At the hearing of the application for permission, the Court may order that — ( a )
-- src:3802 | the application be allowed and where permission is granted to apply for a Prohibiting Order or a Quashing Order, the Court may also order a stay of the proceedings in question until the determination of the application for the Order or until the Court otherwise orders;
-- src:3803 | ( b )
-- src:3804 | the application be dismissed;
-- src:3805 | ( c )
-- src:3806 | the application be served on some other persons; or
-- src:3807 | ( d )
-- src:3808 | further affidavits be filed and served by the parties.
@ref O 24 r 5(9) (src:3801-3808)
GIVEN what IS A `o 24 r 5(9) what the Court may order at the hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(9) the Court may order this at the hearing of the application for permission` MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `o 24 r 5(9)(a) the application be allowed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 24 r 5(9)(b) the application be dismissed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 24 r 5(9)(c) the application be served on some other persons` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 24 r 5(9)(d) further affidavits be filed and served by the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 24 r 5(9) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may order that —" names four things

@ref O 24 r 5(9)(a) (src:3801-3802)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 24 r 2(1) kind of order`
      `permission to apply for the Order is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 5(9)(a) the Court may also order a stay of the proceedings in question until the application for the Order is determined` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `permission to apply for the Order is granted`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "where permission is granted"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 24 r 2(1)(c) a Prohibiting Order` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF kind EQUALS `o 24 r 2(1)(d) a Quashing Order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): the whole condition is "where permission is granted to apply for a Prohibiting Order or a Quashing Order", and a Mandatory Order (or any other order) is outside it

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- Application for Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3810 | 6. —(1) Where permission has been granted to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order, the application for the Order and any included application for a declaration must be made by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained. (2) Unless the summons is filed within 14 days after such permission was granted, the permission lapses.
@ref O 24 r 6(1) (src:3810)
GIVEN `permission has been granted to apply for the Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application and any included application for a declaration are made by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 6(1) the application for the Order is made by summons in the originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `permission has been granted to apply for the Order`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where permission has been granted to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order"
        IF `the application and any included application for a declaration are made by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says how the application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is made another way

-- src:3810 | 6. —(1) Where permission has been granted to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order, the application for the Order and any included application for a declaration must be made by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained. (2) Unless the summons is filed within 14 days after such permission was granted, the permission lapses.
@ref O 24 r 6(2) (src:3810)
`o 24 r 6(2) fourteen days` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 24 r 6(2) (src:3810)
GIVEN `the date the summons was filed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the date it is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 6(2) the permission lapses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the summons was filed`
    WHEN JUST filed THEN
        IF filed AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "Unless the summons is filed within 14 days after such permission was granted, the permission lapses"
        ELSE JUST TRUE -- the summons was filed after the 14 days
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date it is asked about` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- no summons has been filed and the 14 days have run
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the permission lapses "Unless the summons is filed within 14 days", and the 14 days have not run

-- src:3811 | (3) The order granting permission and the summons filed under paragraph (1) must be served on the defendant and the Attorney‑General as soon as is practicable after the filing of the summons and in any case no later than 2 working days after it is filed.
@ref O 24 r 6(3) (src:3811)
GIVEN `the date the order granting permission and the summons were served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `they were served as soon as it was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 24 r 6(3) the order granting permission and the summons are served on the defendant and the Attorney-General in time` MEANS
    `o 24 r 4(2) the document is served as soon as practicable and no later than 2 working days after it is filed` `the date the order granting permission and the summons were served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `they were served as soon as it was practicable`

-- src:3812 | (4) The application mentioned in paragraph (1) must be heard by a Judge.
