-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The duties of Order 24 as regulative rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each rule says the same thing as the decision function named beside it; the decision functions are asserted
-- and the traces are run (a #TRACE prints a result and counts as no assertion on this binary).

DECLARE `o 24 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 24 the applicant`
    `o 24 the defendant`

DECLARE `o 24 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 24 r 2(2) apply for a prerogative order before exhausting every right of appeal or other remedy`
    `o 24 r 4(2) serve the documents on the defendant and the Attorney-General`
    `o 24 r 4(11) comply with the Order for Review of Detention`

-- src:3755 | (2) An application for a prerogative order must not be made before the applicant has exhausted any right of appeal or other remedy provided under any written law.
@ref O 24 r 2(2) (src:3755)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 24 party` `o 24 act`
`o 24 r 2(2) the applicant shall not apply for a prerogative order before exhausting every right of appeal or other remedy` MEANS
    PARTY `o 24 the applicant`
    SHANT `o 24 r 2(2) apply for a prerogative order before exhausting every right of appeal or other remedy`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the applicant applied for a prerogative order before exhausting every right of appeal or other remedy provided under a written law"

-- src:3766 | 4. —(1) The summons for the Order for Review of Detention is to be a summons in the originating application by which the application was made. (2) The originating application without notice, the affidavit supporting the originating application, the order of the Court mentioned in Rule 3(6)( b ), and the summons for the Order for Review of Detention must be served on the defendant and on the Attorney‑General as a non‑party as soon as it is practicable after it is filed and in any case no later than 2 working days after it is filed.
@ref O 24 r 4(2) (src:3766)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 24 party` `o 24 act`
`o 24 r 4(2) the applicant must serve the documents within 2 working days after filing` MEANS
    PARTY `o 24 the applicant`
    MUST `o 24 r 4(2) serve the documents on the defendant and the Attorney-General`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the applicant did not serve the documents on the defendant and the Attorney-General within 2 working days after filing"

-- src:3780 | (11) Where the Court makes an order under paragraph (9)( c ) in the presence of the defendant or the appropriate person or entity, the defendant or that person or entity must comply with the Order for Review of Detention although the Order has not been served.
@ref O 24 r 4(11) (src:3780)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 24 party` `o 24 act`
`o 24 r 4(11) the defendant must comply with the Order for Review of Detention` MEANS
    PARTY `o 24 the defendant`
    MUST `o 24 r 4(11) comply with the Order for Review of Detention`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the defendant did not comply with the Order for Review of Detention, which binds although it has not been served"
